WEBVTT

00:03.836 --> 00:06.430
<i>We now return
to Doctor Who Farted.</i>

00:09.909 --> 00:12.244
Doctor, the alien
attack has begun!

00:12.245 --> 00:14.880
We've got to return
to the 21st century!

00:14.881 --> 00:17.749
Uh... we can't go into
the time machine right now.

00:17.750 --> 00:19.684
But they're going
to kill us all!

00:19.685 --> 00:22.587
All right, all right,
just one second.

00:22.588 --> 00:24.555
So, how was your weekend?

00:28.060 --> 00:29.761
I-Is, is it your line?

00:29.762 --> 00:31.463
I don't...
Uh, no, I don't think so.

00:31.464 --> 00:33.198
I'm-I'm sorry,
whose line is it?

00:33.199 --> 00:35.767
Cut!

00:35.768 --> 00:37.802
That was Peter's line.
Where's Peter?

00:37.803 --> 00:41.106
Sorry, I was in my trailer
eating fancy nuts and smoking.

00:41.107 --> 00:43.942
All right,
everybody, take five.

00:43.943 --> 00:47.712
Okay, I'll be in my dressing
room playing online poker.

00:47.713 --> 00:50.649
That's me asking for help.

00:50.650 --> 00:52.617
Hi, I'm James Woods.

00:52.618 --> 00:54.452
You might know me
from banging your niece

00:54.453 --> 00:56.254
on a pile of your brother's
pool equipment.

00:56.255 --> 00:57.789
<i>Or from Salvador.</i>

00:57.790 --> 00:59.591
But tonight,
I'm here to take you

00:59.592 --> 01:02.294
<i>behind the scenes
on the set of Family Guy.</i>

01:02.295 --> 01:04.496
For the first time ever,
you'll see what a typical

01:04.497 --> 01:08.066
production week is like
for TV's 11th favorite family.

01:08.067 --> 01:10.435
So please join me as we go

01:10.436 --> 01:12.437
<i>Inside Family Guy.</i>

01:37.330 --> 01:39.497
It's certainly not easy
being a family

01:39.498 --> 01:42.300
that also happens to star
in a sitcom together.

01:42.301 --> 01:44.035
Especially last year,
when I discovered

01:44.036 --> 01:45.937
those naked pictures
of that 18-year-old intern

01:45.938 --> 01:47.806
on Peter's phone.

01:47.807 --> 01:49.975
But he explained
that his phone number

01:49.976 --> 01:52.978
was the old number
of-of her ex-boyfriend,

01:52.979 --> 01:55.280
so... what was it again?

01:55.281 --> 01:57.215
Oh, the Cloud, that's right.

01:57.216 --> 01:59.150
So the photos were on the Cloud,

01:59.151 --> 02:02.120
and that the-the Cloud
pulled the pictures or...?

02:02.121 --> 02:05.457
I mean, even if the pictures had
not been sent directly to him,

02:05.458 --> 02:07.692
and that's why he has them.

02:07.693 --> 02:09.628
And-and we both
called the Apple store,

02:09.629 --> 02:11.696
and they said they can't
disprove that it doesn't happen,

02:11.697 --> 02:15.200
so here we are, still married,
still on the show.

02:15.201 --> 02:18.036
A-And it's happened
five times since then,

02:18.037 --> 02:21.906
and some of the pictures had
both Peter and the girl in them.

02:21.907 --> 02:23.575
Being on this show reminds me

02:23.576 --> 02:25.644
<i>of one of my favorite
quotes from Macbeth.</i>

02:25.645 --> 02:27.012
What's the quote?

02:27.013 --> 02:28.079
Whoa!

02:28.080 --> 02:29.547
I didn't realize
this was a trial.

02:29.548 --> 02:31.716
Objection, Your Honor.

02:31.717 --> 02:33.818
Oh, yeah, it's great, you know,
doing a show with your family.

02:33.819 --> 02:35.820
'Cause what guy doesn't
want to go to his office

02:35.821 --> 02:37.055
and have his family there?

02:37.056 --> 02:38.423
You know, and then you
go home after work

02:38.424 --> 02:40.392
and catch up with the family.

02:40.393 --> 02:42.427
- And then, uh,
- next day, same thing.

02:42.428 --> 02:46.331
Just trying to make it to
the weekend, so you can, uh...

02:46.332 --> 02:48.600
spend some time with the family.

02:48.601 --> 02:51.202
Isn't that the dream?

02:51.203 --> 02:52.570
Now, I-I understand the show

02:52.571 --> 02:54.172
was quite different
when it started.

02:54.173 --> 02:57.709
Yeah, in the original pilot,
I was actually the star.

02:57.710 --> 03:01.012
<i>It was called,
CHRIS GRIFFIN: Teen Doctor.</i>

03:01.013 --> 03:04.516
Sir, I'm afraid
I've got some bad news.

03:04.517 --> 03:07.452
Well, it can't be any
worse than what's in here.

03:09.889 --> 03:11.256
I ad-libbed that line.

03:11.257 --> 03:12.891
I wasn't even supposed to talk.

03:12.892 --> 03:14.559
What they didn't know
is that I'd been privately

03:14.560 --> 03:17.028
doing jokes about
the newspaper for years.

03:17.029 --> 03:18.596
But, you know,
it's not just the Griffins

03:18.597 --> 03:21.199
<i>who work hard to make
Family Guy what it is.</i>

03:21.200 --> 03:22.801
Here in the props department,

03:22.802 --> 03:24.669
some sweaty guy
is working on the Petercopter.

03:24.670 --> 03:26.104
That's right.

03:26.105 --> 03:28.640
You know, a lot of people
don't realize SEAL Team Six

03:28.641 --> 03:31.542
actually completed
their mission in this puppy.

03:32.645 --> 03:34.546
<i>Oh, cool, Family Guy!</i>

03:34.547 --> 03:36.580
Over here!
I'm down here!

03:37.983 --> 03:39.117
Knock-knock?

03:39.118 --> 03:40.719
Yeah?
Hi, Stewie.

03:40.720 --> 03:42.821
<i>Hey, I was just showing
the viewers around Family Guy,</i>

03:42.822 --> 03:46.458
and we thought we'd drop in
and talk to you about the show.

03:46.459 --> 03:47.659
You want to talk
about the show?

03:47.660 --> 03:49.461
I'll talk about the show.
The show sucks.

03:49.462 --> 03:51.996
The only reason I stay here
is to maintain my profile

03:51.997 --> 03:55.734
for my start-up business,
DiscreetCrepe.com.

03:55.735 --> 03:57.969
Hi. Are you a straight,
adult male who likes

03:57.970 --> 04:00.238
to eat crepes without people
making unwanted assumptions

04:00.239 --> 04:01.606
about your private life?

04:01.607 --> 04:03.274
Go to DiscreetCrepe.com,

04:03.275 --> 04:05.510
place your order,
and within 30 minutes...

04:08.681 --> 04:11.850
<i>Very masculine pizza delivery
for Stewie Griffin?</i>

04:11.851 --> 04:13.151
Oh, thank you.

04:13.152 --> 04:17.088
Mmm, strawberry-banana Nutella
with raspberry drizzle!

04:17.089 --> 04:19.290
Now I just need a guy's butt
to eat this off of,

04:19.291 --> 04:21.259
and I got myself a night.

04:21.260 --> 04:22.994
<i>But of course,
every episode of Family Guy</i>

04:22.995 --> 04:24.696
starts with the writing.

04:24.697 --> 04:28.165
<i>And here we are...
the Family Guy writers' room...</i>

04:29.435 --> 04:31.870
where the writers
are hard at work

04:31.871 --> 04:33.638
with the show's
talented cast.

04:33.639 --> 04:35.540
Look, don't get me wrong, guys,
I-I think it's hilarious,

04:35.541 --> 04:37.709
and-and I totally get
that the sex thing

04:37.710 --> 04:40.145
is what made me popular,
but would it kill us

04:40.146 --> 04:43.548
to just once tell a joke
that brings glory to God?

04:43.549 --> 04:45.784
Eight years ago, Glenn opened
a restaurant where he was

04:45.785 --> 04:48.052
spying on ladies
peeing in the bathroom.

04:48.053 --> 04:49.988
As part of the class-action
settlement,

04:49.989 --> 04:53.124
he entered rehab,
and that's where he found Jesus.

04:53.125 --> 04:55.527
The restaurant
was called Sprinklers.

04:55.528 --> 04:57.462
That should've been a tip-off.

04:57.463 --> 05:01.199
He still runs Dumpy's, but I'm
pretty sure that one's legit.

05:01.200 --> 05:02.700
<i>As the star of the show,</i>

05:02.701 --> 05:05.537
<i>Peter likes to stay involved
in the writing process.</i>

05:05.538 --> 05:07.372
All right,
butthorns,

05:07.373 --> 05:09.541
which one of you idiots
wrote this script?

05:09.542 --> 05:11.042
Uh, I did.

05:11.043 --> 05:12.911
Oh, what'd you write it,
like, on a computer?

05:12.912 --> 05:13.978
Yeah.

05:13.979 --> 05:15.580
So you know a lot
about computers?

05:15.581 --> 05:17.048
Yeah.

05:17.049 --> 05:19.317
Can you show me how to turn off
the flashlight on my phone?

05:19.318 --> 05:21.219
Don't touch my phone!

05:21.220 --> 05:23.555
And another thing, I read
this piece of garbage script.

05:23.556 --> 05:25.056
It's only one page.

05:25.057 --> 05:26.191
That's never gonna cut it.

05:26.192 --> 05:27.859
Uh, that's
just the cover.

05:27.860 --> 05:30.495
You can turn the page,
like this.

05:30.496 --> 05:32.897
Well, why you hiding all these
pages behind the first page?!

05:32.898 --> 05:34.232
What's wrong with them?!

05:34.233 --> 05:35.834
Stand by your work
or get out!

05:35.835 --> 05:37.335
Now, spit in each
other's mouths.

05:38.904 --> 05:42.073
You know I'm only tough on you
'cause I hate you, right?

05:42.074 --> 05:44.943
Yeah, over the years, Peter's
become just a total nightmare.

05:44.944 --> 05:46.878
I mean, you know,
he's not Jim Belushi.

05:46.879 --> 05:48.913
He's not peeing
in Snapple bottles on set,

05:48.914 --> 05:50.949
which is, like,
a totally real thing.

05:50.950 --> 05:52.784
But he-he's-he's pretty bad.

05:52.785 --> 05:55.186
Dad refuses to interact
with any actors on set.

05:55.187 --> 05:57.088
He'll only rehearse
with helium balloons

05:57.089 --> 05:59.457
with crudely drawn faces
on them.

05:59.458 --> 06:01.092
I'm sorry, Meg,
but you're grounded.

06:01.093 --> 06:03.094
But, Dad,
the prom is tonight. Over.

06:04.430 --> 06:06.130
You heard
your father, Meg. Over.

06:08.133 --> 06:09.801
Peter, you ready
to hit the Drunken Clam?

06:09.802 --> 06:11.870
Over.

06:11.871 --> 06:15.039
It's difficult having to give up
my chair for the balloon.

06:15.040 --> 06:17.575
But that's the business
we call "show."

06:17.576 --> 06:20.211
Excuse me, Joe.

06:20.212 --> 06:22.313
The Fat Man's behavior
has been deteriorating

06:22.314 --> 06:23.615
for quite some time.

06:23.616 --> 06:25.750
And I think someone may have

06:25.751 --> 06:28.887
placed an anonymous phone call
to the network about it.

06:43.402 --> 06:46.137
Word around the stage is they've
decided to finally fire Peter

06:46.138 --> 06:48.006
and replace him
with another actor.

06:48.007 --> 06:49.474
And this time, it's permanent.

06:49.475 --> 06:51.776
Not like when we killed off
Brian for a few episodes,

06:51.777 --> 06:54.913
so he could shoot that crappy
movie... what was it?

06:54.914 --> 06:57.148
<i>It was a remake of Old Yeller
where the dog</i>

06:57.149 --> 06:59.017
gets the drop on him
and kills him first.

06:59.018 --> 07:01.319
I'm sorry.

07:01.320 --> 07:04.489
<i>No, I'm sorry.</i>

07:07.660 --> 07:11.529
They miscalculated the number
of dogs who buy movie tickets.

07:11.530 --> 07:13.331
It's actually
pretty awkward.

07:13.332 --> 07:15.300
I mean, Dad's the only one
in the whole production

07:15.301 --> 07:17.001
who doesn't know
he's being fired.

07:17.002 --> 07:19.603
But he'll find out tomorrow
at the table read.

07:22.675 --> 07:25.343
This is how we did that.

07:25.344 --> 07:27.311
Bet you didn't know.

07:36.388 --> 07:39.223
<i>The table read is where the
Family Guy cast reads aloud</i>

07:39.224 --> 07:41.225
that week's script
to see how the story

07:41.226 --> 07:43.227
and the jokes are working.

07:43.228 --> 07:46.898
And where Peter will learn
he's being written off the show.

07:46.899 --> 07:49.701
Okay, everybody, welcome to
the table read for this week's

07:49.702 --> 07:53.671
episode, entitled, "Peter Dies
(We're Really Serious, No Joke,

07:53.672 --> 07:56.074
He's Dead
and Never Coming Back)."

07:56.075 --> 07:58.076
Oh, and there's other pages.
You got to turn them.

07:58.077 --> 07:59.544
Here, let me show you.

07:59.545 --> 08:01.746
"Interior, Griffins'
living room, day.

08:01.747 --> 08:03.982
"Brian, Meg and Chris watch TV.

08:03.983 --> 08:05.817
Lois enters, upset."

08:05.818 --> 08:07.552
You guys, I have terrible news!

08:07.553 --> 08:09.320
Your father is dead.

08:09.321 --> 08:11.889
He was shot in the head
while killing himself.

08:11.890 --> 08:13.891
I suppose he had his demons.

08:13.892 --> 08:15.593
And his enemies.

08:15.594 --> 08:17.028
Wait, I'm... I'm what?

08:17.029 --> 08:18.396
Oh-oh, I know.

08:18.397 --> 08:20.698
Stewie's gonna fire up
his time machine and undo this.

08:20.699 --> 08:22.100
"Stewie enters."

08:22.101 --> 08:23.334
Brian, bad news.

08:23.335 --> 08:24.936
My time machine got a virus

08:24.937 --> 08:27.405
that causes Dad to die again
if it's ever used.

08:27.406 --> 08:28.740
Oh, wait, you know what?

08:28.741 --> 08:30.575
I-I bet this
is all Chris' dream.

08:30.576 --> 08:32.910
Wow, I am wide awake!

08:32.911 --> 08:34.679
Okay, but there's
no way this is real.

08:34.680 --> 08:37.081
They'd have to bring in
someone to replace me.

08:37.082 --> 08:38.850
"Uncle Ricky,
played by sitcom buzzard

08:38.851 --> 08:40.918
David Spade, enters."

08:40.919 --> 08:42.120
Hi, everybody.

08:42.121 --> 08:44.122
Uncle Ricky!

08:44.123 --> 08:45.923
Hey guys,
a time period called.

08:45.924 --> 08:47.592
They want an object back.

08:49.294 --> 08:51.796
Aw, do we have
to go to Dad's funeral?

08:51.797 --> 08:54.732
Let's just play
with Uncle Ricky instead.

08:54.733 --> 08:55.933
"The family cheers.

08:55.934 --> 08:57.701
They do not miss Peter."

09:01.740 --> 09:03.975
I'm sorry, Peter,
but the production

09:03.976 --> 09:06.577
just can't deal
with all your nonsense anymore.

09:06.578 --> 09:07.712
We're letting you go.

09:07.713 --> 09:09.080
Oh, please,
don't do this!

09:09.081 --> 09:10.581
I'm begging you, just
give me one more chance!

09:10.582 --> 09:13.084
Okay, fine.

09:14.553 --> 09:17.155
All right, that's it,
you're fired!

09:17.156 --> 09:18.923
And you guys are
all okay with this?!

09:18.924 --> 09:20.625
I'm sorry,
sweetheart.

09:20.626 --> 09:22.226
This is painful
for all of us,

09:22.227 --> 09:24.595
but we just don't
see another option.

09:24.596 --> 09:25.963
Yeah, Peter, we love you,

09:25.964 --> 09:27.331
and-and you're
still part of the family,

09:27.332 --> 09:29.467
just not part of the show.

09:29.468 --> 09:30.802
Look, I don't know
who brought this on,

09:30.803 --> 09:32.303
but maybe it's for the best.

09:32.304 --> 09:34.505
All right, fine,
you bastards can fire me,

09:34.506 --> 09:36.974
but at least I'm leaving
with my dignity.

09:53.459 --> 09:53.490
Have a good life, Mr. G.

09:54.993 --> 09:56.529
Your penis is out.

09:57.633 --> 10:00.218
<i>Welcome back
to Inside Family Guy.</i>

10:00.219 --> 10:02.686
I'm your host and angel investor
to the Fappening,

10:02.687 --> 10:04.119
James Woods.

10:04.120 --> 10:05.520
Boy, we picked
quite a week to document

10:05.521 --> 10:08.101
<i>the production
of a Family Guy episode.</i>

10:08.102 --> 10:10.904
Yesterday, Peter Griffin
was fired from the show

10:10.905 --> 10:13.279
and replaced by David Spade.

10:13.280 --> 10:15.448
Given this surprising
development,

10:15.449 --> 10:18.668
we decided to follow Peter,
and see if our cameras

10:18.669 --> 10:21.170
<i>could capture his story,
as well.</i>

10:21.205 --> 10:23.373
<i>We caught up with Peter
at Hollywood's legendary</i>

10:23.374 --> 10:26.142
<i>Chateau Marmont Hotel,
where I once engaged</i>

10:26.143 --> 10:28.691
<i>in the consensual murder
of an underaged prostitute.</i>

10:28.855 --> 10:30.155
So, what's your plan?

10:30.157 --> 10:32.092
Are you going to be
staying here for awhile?

10:32.093 --> 10:33.760
Yeah, well, I figured if
my family doesn't want me

10:33.761 --> 10:36.229
on the show, there's no reason
I should keep living with them.

10:36.230 --> 10:39.232
I-I mean, there's no hard
feelings, um, I just feel like

10:39.233 --> 10:43.036
this is best for me, and this is
best for those cancerous dicks.

10:43.037 --> 10:45.171
And what's next
for Peter Griffin?

10:45.172 --> 10:47.407
Well, starting tomorrow,
I'm getting back out there.

10:47.408 --> 10:49.743
I already got an audition
to be the caring dad

10:49.744 --> 10:51.678
for a Cheerios commercial.

10:51.679 --> 10:52.679
Hey, Dad?

10:52.680 --> 10:53.713
Yeah, bud?

10:53.714 --> 10:54.748
When you were a kid,

10:54.749 --> 10:56.716
what did you want to be
when you grew up?

10:56.717 --> 10:58.585
Well, I wanted
to be a rock star.

10:58.586 --> 11:00.120
Why didn't you
become one?

11:00.121 --> 11:01.387
'Cause of you, bud.

11:01.388 --> 11:03.923
I smiled at one girl
in a cell phone store,

11:03.924 --> 11:05.859
and now here I am,
stuck eating cereal

11:05.860 --> 11:07.060
for dinner with a kid.

11:07.061 --> 11:09.963
You'll always be
a rock star to me, Dad.

11:09.964 --> 11:11.764
You ruined my life.

11:13.601 --> 11:15.534
I'm going to bed.

11:20.808 --> 11:23.810
<i>Wednesdays are rehearsal
days here at Family Guy</i>

11:23.811 --> 11:25.945
and the first rehearsal
with David Spade

11:25.946 --> 11:28.046
appears to be
going very well.

11:30.151 --> 11:31.551
"Uncle Ricky,

11:31.552 --> 11:34.120
what are all these strippers
doing in our house?"

11:34.121 --> 11:36.422
"Uh... each other?"

11:36.423 --> 11:38.458
Hmm?

11:40.461 --> 11:41.828
Oh, my God!

11:41.829 --> 11:43.096
I'm sorry, I just...

11:44.131 --> 11:45.799
Did you see
the way he smirked?

11:45.800 --> 11:48.802
He's like a naughty
53-year-old boy.

11:48.803 --> 11:49.903
Who is this guy?

11:49.904 --> 11:51.171
I'm not familiar with him.

11:51.172 --> 11:53.306
<i>That's David Spade
from Just Shoot Me!</i>

11:53.307 --> 11:54.774
I don't know that one.

11:54.775 --> 11:56.609
<i>He was in Grown Ups,
Joe Dirt,</i>

11:56.610 --> 11:57.944
<i>Saturday Night Live.</i>

11:57.945 --> 11:59.245
Saturday what how?

11:59.246 --> 12:01.347
<i>And he was also in some
movie called Senseless.</i>

12:01.348 --> 12:02.582
With Marlon Wayans?

12:02.583 --> 12:05.819
Oh, yeah, he played
Scott Thorpe.

12:05.820 --> 12:08.454
Donna, I'm here
with Scott Thorpe.

12:08.455 --> 12:10.348
<i>That's right,
from Senseless.</i>

12:14.361 --> 12:16.930
Yeah, I got to be honest,
I'm having a blast.

12:16.931 --> 12:19.165
You know, now that
I'm not tied down by the show,

12:19.166 --> 12:21.835
it's given me more time
to pursue my true passion:

12:21.836 --> 12:24.337
weaving sexually
explicit tapestries

12:24.338 --> 12:25.804
featuring the Minions.

12:30.644 --> 12:33.445
Did you have any questions
about the artist?

12:37.384 --> 12:40.119
<i>Thursdays at Family Guy
are reserved for shooting</i>

12:40.120 --> 12:43.189
all those flashbacks and
cutaway gags we love so much,

12:43.190 --> 12:44.691
and what most people don't know

12:44.692 --> 12:48.127
is that all these gags
are directed by James Cameron.

12:48.128 --> 12:49.629
What's that?

12:49.630 --> 12:50.864
I'm sorry.

12:50.865 --> 12:52.665
Apparently,
I misread the cue card.

12:52.666 --> 12:55.401
They're directed by James,
the cameraman.

12:55.402 --> 12:57.370
Tell us, how'd
you get the gig?

12:57.371 --> 13:00.807
I sell Vicodin to
some of the producers.

13:00.808 --> 13:03.209
What a wonderful
Hollywood story.

13:03.210 --> 13:05.511
You know, many viewers
think our cutaways

13:05.512 --> 13:07.814
are just whipped together,
but they actually

13:07.815 --> 13:11.317
<i>go through a rigorous
testing process before filming.</i>

13:11.318 --> 13:13.720
This is the planet Jew-piter,

13:13.721 --> 13:17.156
and he could say,
"Next year is my star mitzvah."

13:18.592 --> 13:19.659
They love it.

13:19.660 --> 13:21.394
Tell the director.
Where is he?

13:21.395 --> 13:23.830
It says don't take
it with alcohol,

13:23.831 --> 13:25.899
but you should take
it with alcohol.

13:25.900 --> 13:27.066
Yeah, duh.

13:27.067 --> 13:29.736
I also need a couple for
the girl I'm babysitting.

13:29.737 --> 13:33.873
<i>Meanwhile, David Spade is
making lots of friends on set.</i>

13:33.874 --> 13:36.075
Yeah, I'll definitely
talk to the writers.

13:36.076 --> 13:38.111
I agree, there's a lot
about your character

13:38.112 --> 13:39.245
that's still untapped.

13:39.246 --> 13:41.080
Okay, thank you, because,

13:41.081 --> 13:42.849
like, yes, I'm greased-up

13:42.850 --> 13:45.351
and, yes, I'm deaf,
but what else am I?

13:45.352 --> 13:46.352
Totally.

13:46.353 --> 13:47.553
Thanks, man.

13:47.554 --> 13:48.721
Okay, we're ready for you.

13:48.722 --> 13:51.224
I'll be right there.

13:51.225 --> 13:52.892
Who's the new kid?

13:52.893 --> 13:55.094
Hot-chee-wawa!

13:55.095 --> 13:58.698
Unfortunately, things aren't
going quite so well for Peter.

14:00.401 --> 14:04.270
Yeah, it's an '09,
fully loaded, extra cool A/C.

14:04.271 --> 14:05.738
Great.

14:05.739 --> 14:08.374
I just made $500
flipping a Honda.

14:08.375 --> 14:09.976
All I did was
Armor-All the dash.

14:09.977 --> 14:11.277
Boom.

14:14.782 --> 14:16.249
Hey, any mail for me?

14:16.250 --> 14:18.251
Yes, your death
threats to Grimace

14:18.252 --> 14:19.419
have all been returned.

14:19.420 --> 14:21.921
Well, has the Shamrock Shake
period been extended?

14:21.922 --> 14:23.489
I believe that's
still seasonal,

14:23.490 --> 14:25.925
but while I have you,
your bill remains unpaid,

14:25.926 --> 14:28.428
and we saw you selling
our robes on eBay.

14:28.429 --> 14:30.596
I'm afraid we're evicting
you from the hotel.

14:30.597 --> 14:32.265
What's your
home address?

14:32.266 --> 14:33.499
I'm sorry, sir.

14:33.500 --> 14:35.268
Now do you want to
leave the regular way,

14:35.269 --> 14:37.403
or do you want our Uncle
Phil to throw you out?

14:37.404 --> 14:40.106
I think you know
what I want.

14:50.250 --> 14:51.417
Door was unlocked.

14:51.418 --> 14:52.617
I'm sure that's fine.

14:54.955 --> 14:57.190
Well, this seems like
a really cheery place,

14:57.191 --> 14:59.826
and looks like some guy
named Brooks was here,

14:59.827 --> 15:02.195
and I think this is gonna
work out just great.

15:02.196 --> 15:04.364
You don't miss your
show or your family at all?

15:04.365 --> 15:06.099
Of course I miss my family

15:06.100 --> 15:09.435
but everything comes to an end
eventually, a-and you just...

15:09.436 --> 15:11.604
you just got to keep
moving forward.

15:11.605 --> 15:12.939
Are you gonna
be all right?

15:12.940 --> 15:14.340
Oh, yeah, yeah.

15:14.341 --> 15:16.843
I-in fact, I was just about
to melt some cheese on chips

15:16.844 --> 15:19.612
if you want to stay
for a sad, single guy dinner.

15:19.613 --> 15:20.913
You going oven
or microwave?

15:20.914 --> 15:22.181
Uh, microwave.

15:22.182 --> 15:23.749
I don't know how
to turn on the oven.

15:25.219 --> 15:27.687
Those, uh, chips are
gonna be chewy, Peter.

15:32.440 --> 15:35.442
<i>Friday night is tape night
here at Family Guy,</i>

15:35.443 --> 15:39.279
but tonight they'll be filming
the show without Peter Griffin.

15:39.280 --> 15:41.614
I have to admit,
it's a little strange

15:41.615 --> 15:43.283
taping a show without Peter.

15:43.284 --> 15:45.118
It-it just doesn't feel right.

15:45.119 --> 15:47.320
I'm especially going
to miss the Fat Man's bit

15:47.321 --> 15:48.555
with the audience where he fires

15:48.556 --> 15:50.457
the T-shirt cannon
at his own head.

15:50.458 --> 15:53.159
You know he once tried to hold
up a store with that thing?

15:53.160 --> 15:55.228
All right,
everybody on the floor.

15:55.229 --> 15:56.296
Empty the register.

15:56.297 --> 15:57.330
Please, don't do this!

15:57.331 --> 15:58.331
Oh, yeah?

15:58.332 --> 15:59.499
You want to be a hero?

15:59.500 --> 16:01.401
Here's what
happens to heroes.

16:01.402 --> 16:03.136
Anybody else want
to be a hero?

16:03.137 --> 16:04.204
Ooh, me, me, me!

16:04.205 --> 16:05.805
Over here!
Over here!

16:05.806 --> 16:08.375
And with regard
to Peter's replacement, well,

16:08.376 --> 16:10.643
as his parents and
previous co-stars have learned,

16:10.644 --> 16:14.080
a little of David Spade
goes a long way.

16:14.081 --> 16:16.316
David, the line is,
"What's for dinner?"

16:16.317 --> 16:17.484
Go again.

16:17.485 --> 16:19.519
What's for dinner?

16:19.520 --> 16:21.254
Hmm?

16:22.256 --> 16:23.823
Okay, we can trim
that in editing.

16:23.824 --> 16:25.525
He's getting on people's nerves.

16:25.526 --> 16:28.728
I mean, there's only so many
jars I can open for one man.

16:28.729 --> 16:30.830
Lois, I want pickles!

16:30.831 --> 16:32.065
Coming!

16:32.066 --> 16:35.168
He has tiny hands
but when one of my rings

16:35.169 --> 16:37.370
went down the drain,
he got it right out.

16:37.371 --> 16:39.239
<i>Meanwhile, Peter has wound up</i>

16:39.240 --> 16:41.741
<i>here at the Chinese Theatre,
where panhandlers</i>

16:41.742 --> 16:43.777
<i>dress up like
iconic movie characters</i>

16:43.778 --> 16:45.945
<i>and charge tourists for photos.</i>

16:45.946 --> 16:48.248
<i>It's even seedier
than it sounds.</i>

16:48.249 --> 16:49.783
Step right up,
get your picture taken

16:49.784 --> 16:52.352
with beloved comic
icon, Little Lotta.

16:52.353 --> 16:53.319
Just two dollars.

16:53.320 --> 16:54.354
Who are you?

16:54.355 --> 16:55.522
Uh, Little Lotta?

16:55.523 --> 16:57.290
She was friends
with Audrey and Dot.

16:57.291 --> 16:58.691
Never heard of her.

17:05.533 --> 17:07.233
That's it.
Screw this.

17:07.234 --> 17:10.502
I am taking back my TV show
and my family.

17:12.640 --> 17:14.873
Ah, we just missed her.

17:18.446 --> 17:21.281
Hey, Smitty, I'm here
to get my show back.

17:21.282 --> 17:23.883
I'm sorry, Mr. Griffin,
but we have specific orders

17:23.884 --> 17:25.418
not to let you
onto the lot.

17:25.419 --> 17:26.486
Seriously?

17:26.487 --> 17:28.221
Well, I suppose,
you could come inside

17:28.222 --> 17:29.589
if you had an
idea for a show

17:29.590 --> 17:31.223
the heads of the
network wanted to buy.

17:32.393 --> 17:34.260
<i>Bumblr with a Tumblr.</i>

17:34.261 --> 17:35.295
So, you see, he's got

17:35.296 --> 17:37.397
a Tumblr account
and he's clumsy.

17:37.398 --> 17:39.632
We really like the idea
that the words rhyme.

17:39.633 --> 17:42.068
Absolutely,
but just a thought:

17:42.069 --> 17:44.571
what if he doesn't bumble?

17:44.572 --> 17:47.340
Um... I-I guess so.

17:47.341 --> 17:50.109
And are we married
to the Tumblr account?

17:50.110 --> 17:53.313
They bought the pitch, but, um,
after a series of network notes,

17:53.314 --> 17:56.749
<i>Bumblr with a Tumblr eventually
aired as Bamblr with a Famblr,</i>

17:56.750 --> 18:00.153
which made sense to nobody and
is now in its third season.

18:00.154 --> 18:02.322
It did also get me on the lot.

18:02.323 --> 18:04.257
All right,
stop the show!

18:04.258 --> 18:05.258
Dad!

18:05.259 --> 18:06.626
That's right,
I'm back!

18:06.627 --> 18:09.095
And, Chris, I brought you
a T-shirt of Kermit the Frog

18:09.096 --> 18:10.430
acting like a hip-hop guy.

18:10.431 --> 18:11.998
That's so dope.

18:11.999 --> 18:13.633
Don't put it on.
It'll fall apart,

18:13.634 --> 18:16.503
but listen, everybody,
I realized something.

18:16.504 --> 18:19.439
I've been a real jerk...
to you guys, and to all

18:19.440 --> 18:21.274
the union fat asses
that I assume do something

18:21.275 --> 18:22.675
to keep this thing going.

18:22.676 --> 18:25.912
The fact is, I got
too big for my britches,

18:25.913 --> 18:29.349
but I know now that I'm
nothing without all of you.

18:29.350 --> 18:31.117
Aw, that's nice
of you to say.

18:31.118 --> 18:33.319
Thank you, Stewie,
who I can understand,

18:33.320 --> 18:36.890
and if you guys can find it
in your hearts to take me back,

18:36.891 --> 18:39.359
well, then I promise that
every day I'll prove to you

18:39.360 --> 18:43.029
how much the show, and how much
my family, means to me.

18:43.030 --> 18:44.130
Oh, Peter.

18:44.131 --> 18:46.366
Of course we'll take you back.

18:46.367 --> 18:48.468
Oh, welcome back, buddy.

18:48.469 --> 18:49.869
We missed you so much.

18:49.870 --> 18:54.040
My online poker problem
is burning like a wildfire.

18:54.041 --> 18:55.542
Well, there's
only one problem.

18:55.543 --> 18:56.576
What's that?

18:56.577 --> 18:58.545
What are we gonna do
about David Spade?

18:58.546 --> 19:00.380
Don't worry, I already
took care of that.

19:00.381 --> 19:02.815
I got SofГ­a Vergara deported.

19:02.816 --> 19:05.718
Hey, everyone,
cuchi, cuchi.

19:05.719 --> 19:07.487
I'm your mother now.

19:07.488 --> 19:09.422
So, all right,
let's do a show.

19:09.423 --> 19:11.391
Oh, wait,
if my character's still alive,

19:11.392 --> 19:13.192
that means we don't have
a script to shoot.

19:13.193 --> 19:14.394
Oh, look at this.

19:14.395 --> 19:15.895
We just happen to have

19:15.896 --> 19:18.164
a whole extra
script right here.

19:18.165 --> 19:19.599
"Pete, Don't
Fail Me Now."

19:20.668 --> 19:22.669
Sounds like I might
be a teacher.

19:22.670 --> 19:25.171
Oh, I have a goatee up
till the first commercial,

19:25.172 --> 19:26.739
and then I'm a teacher.

19:26.740 --> 19:28.608
Every week, Peter becomes a diva

19:28.609 --> 19:31.544
so the writers write
a fake script, killing him off.

19:31.545 --> 19:34.213
He storms out,
then by Friday's taping,

19:34.214 --> 19:37.250
comes crawling back,
and we shoot the real script.

19:37.251 --> 19:39.052
Of course,
he always forgets by Monday,

19:39.053 --> 19:41.287
and then he becomes
a pain in the ass again.

19:41.288 --> 19:43.556
Does it bother me that
he does this every week?

19:43.557 --> 19:47.460
Uh, why don't you ask my Camaro?

19:47.461 --> 19:50.930
<i>So, I guess this actually
was a very typical week</i>

19:50.931 --> 19:52.699
<i>on the set of Family Guy.</i>

19:52.700 --> 19:54.233
<i>Thanks for joining us.</i>

19:54.234 --> 19:57.303
<i>I'm James Woods, and we'll
close tonight with a supercut</i>

19:57.304 --> 19:59.906
<i>of every time in the show's
history that Peter got hit</i>

19:59.907 --> 20:01.908
<i>in the crotch
with a bag of nickels.</i>

20:01.909 --> 20:03.209
Ow!

20:05.312 --> 20:06.646
Damn it.

20:06.647 --> 20:07.647
Oh!

20:09.249 --> 20:10.283
Why?!

20:10.284 --> 20:11.618
Hey, Lois, you should do

20:11.619 --> 20:12.619
that thing that
I like...

20:12.620 --> 20:13.720
Hey, kids, have you
seen my wallet?

20:13.721 --> 20:14.887
Oh, nickels!

20:14.888 --> 20:16.723
Son of a bitch!

20:16.724 --> 20:17.757
Uh, ladies and gentlemen,

20:17.758 --> 20:19.125
we have now reached
our cruising...

20:19.126 --> 20:20.126
Ah, damn it!

20:20.127 --> 20:21.794
Boy, can't beat
this weather...

20:21.795 --> 20:23.396
Who is that kid?

20:24.965 --> 20:26.065
Hello?

20:26.066 --> 20:27.266
Uh, hang on, I'll check.

20:27.267 --> 20:28.901
Phone call for
"a bag of nickels"?

20:31.639 --> 20:33.106
At least he was alone.

20:33.107 --> 20:34.641
They usually travel in threes.

20:34.642 --> 20:36.142
Ow! Crap.

20:36.143 --> 20:38.144
B-B-B-Bird, bird, bird,
b-b-b-bird...

20:38.145 --> 20:39.312
Ah, nickels!

20:42.983 --> 20:44.083
Oh, damn it!

20:44.084 --> 20:45.785
Do you think I'm ever
gonna be able to have...

20:48.107 --> 20:48.987
Ow!

20:49.034 --> 20:53.104
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru